Also I believe that we could generate the name in the native code, as all we need to do is: generate the name, call `shm_open` and call `shm_unlink` right after that

https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/a24364a09d9aea98b545f16689a53bafc6b18c14/src/libraries/System.IO.MemoryMappedFiles/src/System/IO/MemoryMappedFiles/MemoryMappedFile.Unix.cs#L213-L216

Could also be written as 
```c#
const int MaxNameLength = 30;
const string NamePrefix = "/dotnet_";
Span<char> guid = stackalloc char[32];
Guid.NewGuid().TryFormat(guid, out int charsWritten, "N");
Debug.Assert(charsWritten == 32);
return $"{NamePrefix}{guid[..(MaxNameLength - NamePrefix.Length)]}";
```

Besides that: must it be based on Guid? We just need something random (of length 22).
